ABSTRACT CLASS

1. Declared using abstract keyword.

2. Can have:
   → Abstract methods
   → Concrete methods
   → Variables
   → Constructors

3. Cannot create an object directly.

   Vehicle v = new Vehicle();  // ❌

4. Child class must implement/override abstract methods.

5. An abstract class can have constructors.

6. Abstract class supports inheritance using extends.

7. A class can extend only ONE class.